Ans-3:
User enters a URL (e.g., https://www.wikipedia.org).

DNS lookup: The browser finds the IP address of the web server hosting the site.

HTTP/HTTPS Request: The browser sends a request to the server for the web page.

Server Response: The server returns an HTML file (and possibly CSS, JS, images).

Rendering Process:

Browser reads HTML → builds DOM (Document Object Model).

Downloads and applies CSS → builds CSSOM.

Executes JavaScript → manipulates the DOM.

Finally, renders the page on the screen.

 Example:
When you open YouTube, the browser:

Fetches HTML → structure of the page

Fetches CSS → colors and layout

Executes JS → plays video and handles likes/comments dynamically.

