Ans-5:
A web server is software (and sometimes hardware) that receives HTTP requests from clients (browsers) and sends back web content (HTML, CSS, images, etc.).
Examples of Web Servers:

Apache HTTP Server — open-source, widely used.

Nginx — known for speed and handling multiple requests.

Microsoft IIS — used with Windows servers.

Node.js (Express) — JavaScript-based server for dynamic sites.

LiteSpeed — optimized for high-performance sites.
Example:
When you open amazon.in, your browser connects to Amazon’s Nginx servers, which send back the HTML and data to load the page.


