Five Popular Web Browsers & Rendering Engines

Google Chrome	Blink	Fast, modern, used in many Chromium-based browsers.
Mozilla Firefox	Gecko	Open-source, highly customizable.
Microsoft Edge	Blink	Based on Chromium, faster than old EdgeHTML.
Safari (Apple)	WebKit	Optimized for Apple devices.
Opera	Blink	Uses same engine as Chrome, adds built-in VPN & tools.

Rendering Engine Difference:
A rendering engine reads HTML, CSS, and JS and draws the webpage.
Different engines interpret styles slightly differently — that’s why sites may look a bit different in Chrome vs Safari.

